{"name":"Kingfisher Daisy","hex":"#583580","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kingfisher daisy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The flowering plant Felicia bergeriana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kingfisher_daisy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Felicia bergeriana","blocks":[{"text":"Felicia bergeriana is a richly branching, hairy annual plant of up to 25 cm (10 in) high that is assigned to the family Asteraceae. It has opposite leaves and flower heads set individually on up to 8 cm long stalks, that consist of an involucre of about 1⁄2 cm diameter with two whorls of bracts, about twelve blue ray florets surrounding more yellow disc florets. It is sometimes called kingfisher daisy in English. It can be found in the Northern and Western Cape provinces of South Africa. It is sometimes cultivated as an ornamental."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Felicia_bergeriana0.jpg/330px-Felicia_bergeriana0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Felicia_bergeriana","wikidata":"Q15598583"},{"title":"Kingfisher","blocks":[{"text":"Kingfishers are a family, the Alcedinidae, of small to medium-sized, brightly coloured birds in the order Coraciiformes. They have a cosmopolitan distribution: most species live in the tropical regions of Africa, Asia, and Oceania, but they can also be found in Europe and the Americas. They can be found in deep forests near calm ponds and small rivers. The family contains 118 species and is divided into three subfamilies and 19 genera. All kingfishers have large heads, long, sharp, pointed bills, short legs, and stubby tails. Most species have bright plumage with only small differences between the sexes. Most species are tropical in distribution, and a slight majority are found only in forests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten.jpg/330px-Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingfisher","wikidata":"Q8154335"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Felicia_bergeriana_Helme_1.jpg/500px-Felicia_bergeriana_Helme_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Felicia_bergeriana_Helme_1.jpg/1280px-Felicia_bergeriana_Helme_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Felicia_bergeriana_Helme_1.jpg/500px-Felicia_bergeriana_Helme_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFelicia_bergeriana_Helme_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Kingfisher_range.png/500px-Kingfisher_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Kingfisher_range.png/1280px-Kingfisher_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Kingfisher_range.png/500px-Kingfisher_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKingfisher_range.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Brown-headed_Paradise-Kingfisher.jpg/500px-Brown-headed_Paradise-Kingfisher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Brown-headed_Paradise-Kingfisher.jpg/1280px-Brown-headed_Paradise-Kingfisher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/